{
  "title": "42: al-Shooraa الشورى",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nحٰمٓ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa-Mim \nعٓسٓقٓ‏(2)\nA’AASAAQAA.\n'Ain. Sin. Qaf. \nكَذٰلِكَ يُوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْكَ وَاِلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَۙ اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(3)\nKAZAALEKA YOOHEAA ELAYKA WA ELAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKA LAAHO A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nThus doth (He) send inspiration to thee as (He did) to those before thee, Allah, Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom. \nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(4)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ WA HOWA A’LIYYUL A’ZEEM.\nTo Him belongs all that is in the heavens and on earth: and He is Most High, Most Great. \nتَكَادُ السَّمٰوٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْ فَوْقِهِنَّ‌ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ لِمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(5)\nTAKAADO AS-SAMAAWAATU YATAFATTARNA MIN FAWQEHENNA WAL MALAAA-EKATO YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WAYASTAGHFEROONA LEMAN-Y FIL ARZ ALAA INNAL LAAHA HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nThe heavens are almost rent asunder from above them (by Him Glory): and the angels celebrate the Praises of their Lord, and pray for forgiveness for (all) beings on earth: Behold! Verily Allah is He, the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ اللّٰهُ حَفِيْظٌ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ۖ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(6)\nWAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA LAAHO HAFEEZUN A’LAYHIM WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nAnd those who take as protectors others besides Him, Allah doth watch over them; and thou art not the disposer of their affairs. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّتُنْذِرَ اُمَّ الْقُرٰى وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا وَتُنْذِرَ يَوْمَ الْجَمْعِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ فَرِيْقٌ فِى الْجَنَّةِ وَفَرِيْقٌ فِى السَّعِيْرِ‏(7)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LLETUNZERA AUMMA KORAA WA MAN HAWLAHAA WATUNZERA YAWMA AL-JAME’E LAA RAYBA FEEH FAREEQUM FIL JANNAH WA FAREEQUM FIL SA-E’ER.\nThus have We sent by inspiration to thee an Arabic Qur'an: that thou mayest warn the Mother of Cities and all around her, and warn (them) of the Day of Assembly, of which there is no doubt: (when) some will be in the Garden, and some in the Blazing Fire. \nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَهُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ يُّدْخِلُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ؕ وَالظّٰلِمُوْنَ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(8)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAA’ALAHUM UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LAAKIL YUDKHELO MAN YASHAAA-O FEE RAHMATEH WA ZAALEMOON MAA LAHUM MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nIf Allah had so willed, He could have made them a single people; but He admits whom He will to His Mercy; and the Wrong-doers will have no protector nor helper. \nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ۚ فَاللّٰهُ هُوَ الْوَلِىُّ وَهُوَ يُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(9)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA FAL-LAAHO HOWA AL-WALEAAAU WA HOWA LAAHUL MAWTAA WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nWhat! Have they taken (for worship) protectors besides Him? But it is Allah, He is the Protector, and it is He Who gives life to the dead: It is He Who has power over all things, \nوَمَا اخْتَلَفْتُمْ فِيْهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ فَحُكْمُهٗۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبِّىْ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُۖ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ‏(10)\nWA MAA AKHTALAFTUM FEEHE MIN SHAY-IN FAHUKMUH ELAL LAAHE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBEE A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE AUNEEBU.\nWhatever it be wherein ye differ, the decision thereof is with Allah: such is Allah my Lord: In Him I trust, and to Him I turn. \nفَاطِرُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا وَّ مِنَ الْاَنْعَامِ اَزْوَاجًا‌ ۚ يَذْرَؤُكُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهٖ شَىْءٌ ‌ۚ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(11)\nFAATERU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ JA-A’LA LAKUM MIN ANFOSEKUM AZWAAJANW WA MENAL AL-AANA’AAME AZWAAJANW YAZRAUKUM FEEHE LAYSA KAMESLEH SHAY-UN WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\n(He is) the Creator of the heavens and the earth: He has made for you pairs from among yourselves, and pairs among cattle: by this means does He multiply you: there is nothing whatever like unto Him, and He is the One that hears and sees (all things). \nلَهٗ مَقَالِيْدُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ۚ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(12)\nLAHU MAQAALEEDU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAHU BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nTo Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth: He enlarges and restricts. The Sustenance to whom He will: for He knows full well all things. \nشَرَعَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الدِّيْنِ مَا وَصّٰى بِهٖ نُوْحًا وَّالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ وَمَا وَصَّيْنَا بِهٖۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَمُوْسٰى وَعِيْسٰٓى اَنْ اَقِيْمُوا الدِّيْنَ وَ لَا تَتَفَرَّقُوْا فِيْهِ‌ؕ كَبُرَ عَلَى الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ مَا تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ اَللّٰهُ يَجْتَبِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ مَنْ يُّنِيْبُ‏(13)\nSHARAA’A LAKUM MENAL DEENE MAA WASSAA BEHI ARSALNAA WWAALLAZEAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA WA MAA WASSAYNAA BEHI IBRAAHEEMA WA MOOSAA WAE’EESAAA AN AAQEEMOOA DEENA WA LAA TATAFARRAQOOA FEEH KABURA A’LAL MUSHREKEEN MAA TADU’OOHUM ELAYHE ALLAAHO YAJTABEAA ELAYHE MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE ELAYHE MAN YYUNEEBU.\nThe same religion has He established for you as that which He enjoined on Noah - the which We have sent by inspiration to thee - and that which We enjoined on Abraham, Moses, and Jesus: Namely, that ye should remain steadfast in religion, and make no divisions therein: to those who worship other things than Allah, hard is the (way) to which thou callest them. Allah chooses to Himself those whom He pleases, and guides to Himself those who turn (to Him). \nوَمَا تَفَرَّقُوْۤا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ بَغْيًاۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى لَّقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْرِثُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(14)\nWA MAA TAFARRAQOOA ILLAA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO BAGHYAN BAYNAHUM WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA ELAA ELAA AJALIM LLAQUZEAAA BAYNAHUM WA INNAL LAZEENA AOORESOOA KETAABA MIN BA’DEHIM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nAnd they became divided only after Knowledge reached them, through selfish envy as between themselves. Had it not been for a Word that went forth before from thy Lord, (tending) to a Term appointed, the matter would have been settled between them: But truly those who have inherited the Book after them are in suspicious (disquieting) doubt concerning it. \nفَلِذٰلِكَ فَادْعُ‌ ۚ وَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَاۤ اُمِرْتَ‌ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ۚ وَقُلْ اٰمَنْتُ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ كِتٰبٍ‌‌ۚ وَاُمِرْتُ لِاَعْدِلَ بَيْنَكُمُ‌ؕ اَللّٰهُ رَبُّنَا وَرَبُّكُمْ‌ؕ لَنَاۤ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْ‌ۚ لَا حُجَّةَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمُ‌ؕ اَللّٰهُ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا‌ۚ وَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُؕ‏(15)\nFALEZAALEKA FAD-O’ WAASTAQEM KAMAA AUMERTA WA LAA TATTABEA’ AHWAAA-AHUM WA QUL AAMANTO BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO MIN KETAABIM WA AN A-A’BODA LEAAA’DELA BAYNAKUMU ALLAAHO RABBONAA WARABBUKUM LANAA A-A’MAALONAA WA LAKUM A-A’MAALOKUM LAA HUJJATA BAYNANAA WABAYNAKUMU ALLAAHO YAJMAU’U BAYNANAA WA ELAYHE AL-MASEERU.\nNow then, for that (reason), call (them to the Faith), and stand steadfast as thou art commanded, nor follow thou their vain desires; but say: “I believe in the Book which Allah has sent down; and I am commanded to judge justly between you. Allah is our Lord and your Lord: for us (is the responsibility for) our deeds, and for you for your deeds. There is no contention between us and you. Allah will bring us together, and to Him is (our) Final Goal. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُحَآجُّوْنَ فِى اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا اسْتُجِيْبَ لَهٗ حُجَّتُهُمْ دَاحِضَةٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَلَيْهِمْ غَضَبٌ وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(16)\nWAL LAZEENA YUHAAJJOONA FIL LAAHE MIN BA’DE MAA ASTUJEEBA LAHU HUJJATUHUM DAAHEZATUN I’NDAL RABBEHIM WA A’LAYHIM GHAZABUN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN.\nBut those who dispute concerning Allah after He has been accepted, futile is their dispute in the Sight of their Lord: on them will be a Penalty terrible. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ وَالْمِيْزَانَ‌ؕ وَمَا يُدْرِيْكَ لَعَلَّ السَّاعَةَ قَرِيْبٌ‏(17)\nALLAAHO LAZEE ANZALAL KETAABA BIL-HAQQE WAL MEEZAANA WA MAA YUDREEKA LA-A’LLAS SAA-A’TA QAREEB.\nIt is Allah Who has sent down the Book in Truth, and the Balance (by which to weigh conduct). And what will make thee realise that perhaps the Hour is close at hand? \nيَسْتَعْجِلُ بِهَا الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهَا‌ ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مُشْفِقُوْنَ مِنْهَا ۙ وَيَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهَا الْحَقُّ ‌ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُمَارُوْنَ فِى السَّاعَةِ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(18)\nYASTAA’JELU BEHAA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BEHAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MUSHFEQOONA MINHAA WA YA’LAMOON AANNAHAA HAQQO ALAA INNAL LAZEENA YUMAAROONA FIL AS-SAAA’ATE LAFEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nOnly those wish to hasten it who believe not in it: those who believe hold it in awe, and know that it is the Truth. Behold, verily those that dispute concerning the Hour are far astray. \nاَللّٰهُ لَطِيْفٌۢ بِعِبَادِهٖ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْقَوِىُّ الْعَزِيْزُ‏(19)\nALLAAHO LATEEFUN BE-E’BAADEHI YARZOQO MAN YASHAAA-O WA HOWA QAWIYYUL A’ZEEZUL.\nGracious is Allah to His servants: He gives Sustenance to whom He pleases: and He has power and can carry out His Will. \nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ حَرْثَ الْاٰخِرَةِ نَزِدْ لَهٗ فِىْ حَرْثِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ حَرْثَ الدُّنْيَا نُؤْتِهٖ مِنْهَا وَمَا لَهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنْ نَّصِيْبٍ‏(20)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO HARSA AAKHERATE NAZED LAHU FEE HARSEH WA MAN KAANA YOREEDO HARSA DUNYAA NUTEH MINHAA WA MAA LAHU FIL AAKHERATE MIN NNASEEBIN.\nTo any that desires the tilth of the Hereafter, We give increase in his tilth, and to any that desires the tilth of this world, We grant somewhat thereof, but he has no share or lot in the Hereafter. \nاَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكٰٓؤُا شَرَعُوْا لَهُمْ مِّنَ الدِّيْنِ مَا لَمْ يَاْذَنْۢ بِهِ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةُ الْفَصْلِ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(21)\nAM LAHUM SHURAKAAAUA SHARAU’OOA LAHUM MENAL DEENE MAA LAM YAAZAN BEHIL LAAH WA LAWLAA KALEMATU FASLE LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM WA INNA ZAALEMEEN LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nWhat! have they partners (in godhead), who have established for them some religion without the permission of Allah? Had it not been for the Decree of Judgment, the matter would have been decided between them (at once). But verily the Wrong-doers will have a grievous Penalty. \nتَرَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ مُشْفِقِيْنَ مِمَّا كَسَبُوْا وَهُوَ وَاقِعٌۢ بِهِمْ‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فِىْ رَوْضَاتِ الْجَنّٰتِ‌ۚ لَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(22)\nTARAL ZAALEMEEN MUSHFEQEENA MIMMAA KASABOO WA HOWA WAAQEA’UN BEHIM WA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FEE RAWZAATE AL-JANNAATE LAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM ZAALEKA HOWA FAZLUL AL-KABEERU.\nThou wilt see the Wrong-doers in fear on account of what they have earned, and (the burden of) that must (necessarily) fall on them. But those who believe and work righteous deeds will be in the luxuriant meads of the Gardens: they shall have, before their Lord, all that they wish for. That will indeed be the magnificent Bounty (of Allah). \nذٰ لِكَ الَّذِىْ يُبَشِّرُ اللّٰهُ عِبَادَهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ‌ؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا اِلَّا الْمَوَدَّةَ فِى الْقُرْبٰى‌ؕ وَمَنْ يَّقْتَرِفْ حَسَنَةً نَّزِدْ لَهٗ فِيْهَا حُسْنًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ شَكُوْرٌ‏(23)\nZAA LEKA LAZEE YUBASSHERU LAAHO E’EBAADAHU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS AS-SAALEHAATE QUL LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN ILLAA AL-MAWADDATA FIL AL-QURBAA WA MAN YYAQTAREF HASANATANW NNAZED LAHU FEEHAA HUSNANW INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR SHAKOORUN.\nThat is (the Bounty) whereof Allah gives Glad Tidings to His Servants who believe and do righteous deeds. Say: “No reward do I ask of you for this except the love of those near of kin.” And if any one earns any good, We shall give him an increase of good in respect thereof: for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (service). \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا‌ ۚ فَاِنْ يَّشَاِ اللّٰهُ يَخْتِمْ عَلٰى قَلْبِكَ‌ ؕ وَيَمْحُ اللّٰهُ الْبَاطِلَ وَيُحِقُّ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖۤ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(24)\nAM YAQOOLOONA TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN FA-IN YYASHAA LAAHO YAKHTEM A’LAA QALBEKA WAYAMHU LAAHO AL-BAATELA WAYUHEQQU HAQQA BEKALEMAATEH INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nWhat! Do they say, “He has forged a falsehood against Allah”? But if Allah willed, He could seal up thy heart. And Allah blots out Vanity, and proves the Truth by His Words. For He knows well the secrets of all hearts. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنِ السَّيِّاٰتِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ ۙ‏(25)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YAQBALU AT-TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI WAYAA’FOOA A’NIL SAYYE-AATE YA’LAMO MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nHe is the One that accepts repentance from His Servants and forgives sins: and He knows all that ye do. \nوَيَسْتَجِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَيَزِيْدُهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ؕ وَالْكٰفِرُوْنَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(26)\nWAYASTAJEEBU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAYAZEEDUHUM MIN FAZLEH KAAFEROONA LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN.\nAnd He listens to those who believe and do deeds of righteousness, and gives them increase of His Bounty: but for the Unbelievers their is a terrible Penalty. \nوَلَوْ بَسَطَ اللّٰهُ الرِّزْقَ لِعِبَادِهٖ لَبَغَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلٰكِنْ يُّنَزِّلُ بِقَدَرٍ مَّا يَشَآءُ ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(27)\nWA LAW BASATA LAAHO RIZQA LE-E’BAADEHI LABAGHAWA FIL ARZE WA LAAKIL YYUNAZZELU BEQADARIN MAA YASHAAA INNAHU BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERUM BASEER.\nIf Allah were to enlarge the provision for His Servants, they would indeed transgress beyond all bounds through the earth; but he sends (it) down in due measure as He pleases. For He is with His Servants Well-acquainted, Watchful. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُنَزِّلُ الْغَيْثَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا قَنَطُوْا وَيَنْشُرُ رَحْمَتَهٗ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْوَلِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(28)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YUNAZZELU AL-GHAYSA MIN BA’DE MAA QANATOOA WAYANSHURU RAHMATAH WA HOWA AL-WALEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nHe is the One that sends down rain (even) after (men) have given up all hope, and scatters His Mercy (far and wide). And He is the Protector, Worthy of all Praise. \nوَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِهٖ خَلْقُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَثَّ فِيْهِمَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ عَلٰى جَمْعِهِمْ اِذَا يَشَآءُ قَدِيْرٌ‏(29)\nWA MIN AAYAATEHI KHALQUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BASSA FEEHEMAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL WA HOWA A’LAA JAME’EHEM EZAA YASHAAA QADEER.\nAnd among His Signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the living creatures that He has scattered through them: and He has power to gather them together when He wills. \nوَمَاۤ اَصَابَكُمْ مِّنْ مُّصِيْبَةٍ فَبِمَا كَسَبَتْ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنْ كَثِيْرٍؕ‏(30)\nWA MAA AASAABAKUM MIN MMUSEEBATIN FA BEMAA KASABAT AYDEEKUM WAYAA’FOOA A’N KASEERIN.\nWhatever misfortune happens to you, is because on the things your hands have wrought, and for many (of them) He grants forgiveness. \nوَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ۖۚ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(31)\nWA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nNor can ye frustrate (aught), (fleeing) through the earth; nor have ye, besides Allah, any one to protect or to help. \nوَمِنْ اٰيٰتِهِ الْجَوَارِ فِى الْبَحْرِ كَالْاَعْلَامِؕ‏(32)\nWA MIN AAAYAATEHE JAWAARIL FIL BAHRE KAALAAA’LAAME.\nAnd among His Signs are the ships, smooth-running through the ocean, (tall) as mountains. \nاِنْ يَّشَاْ يُسْكِنِ الرِّيْحَ فَيَظْلَلْنَ رَوَاكِدَ عَلٰى ظَهْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍۙ‏(33)\nIN YYASHAA YUSKENE AR-REEHA FAYAZLALNA RAWAAKEDA A’LAA ZAHREH INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nIf it be His Will He can still the Wind: then would they become motionless on the back of the (ocean). Verily in this are Signs for everyone who patiently perseveres and is grateful. \nاَوْ يُوْبِقْهُنَّ بِمَا كَسَبُوْا وَيَعْفُ عَنْ كَثِيْرٍ‏(34)\nAW YOOBEQHUNNA BEMAA KASABOO WAYAA’FU A’N KASEERIM.\nOr He can cause them to perish because of the (evil) which (the men) have earned; but much doth He forgive. \nوَّيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا ؕ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(35)\nWWAYAA’LAMA LAZEENA YUJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATENAA MAA LAHUM MIN MAHEES.\nBut let those know, who dispute about Our Signs, that there is for them no way of escape. \nفَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَمَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ۚ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَۚ‏(36)\nFAMAA MAA OOTEETUM MIN SHAY-IN FAMATAAUL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN LILLAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nWhatever ye are given (here) is (but) a convenience of this life: but that which is with Allah is better and more lasting: (it is) for those who believe and put their trust in their Lord: \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفَوَاحِشَ وَاِذَا مَا غَضِبُوْا هُمْ يَغْفِرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(37)\nWAL LAZEENA YAJTANEBOONA KABAAAERA AL-AESME WAL FAWAAHESHA WA EZAA MAA GHAZEBOOA HUM YAGHFEROONA.\nThose who avoid the greater crimes and shameful deeds, and, when they are angry even then forgive; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَاَقَامُوْا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَمْرُهُمْ شُوْرٰى بَيْنَهُمْ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(38)\nWAL LAZEENA ASTAJAABOOA LE-RABBEHIM WAAQAAMOOA SALAATA WAAMRUHUM SHOORAA BAYNAHUM WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nThose who hearken to their Lord, and establish regular Prayer; who (conduct) their affairs by mutual Consultation; who spend out of what We bestow on them for Sustenance; \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَاۤ اَصَابَهُمُ الْبَغْىُ هُمْ يَنْتَصِرُوْنَ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA AASAABAHUMU AL-BAGHAAU HUM YANTASEROONA.\nAnd those who, when an oppressive wrong is inflicted on them, (are not cowed but) help and defend themselves. \nوَجَزٰٓؤُا سَيِّئَةٍ سَيِّئَةٌ مِّثْلُهَا‌ۚ فَمَنْ عَفَا وَاَصْلَحَ فَاَجْرُهٗ عَلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(40)\nWAJAZAAAUA SAYATIN SAYYE-ATUM MMESLUHAA FAMAN A’AFAA WAASLAHA FA AJROHU A’LAL LAAH INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL ZAALEMEEN.\nThe recompense for an injury is an injury equal thereto (in degree): but if a person forgives and makes reconciliation, his reward is due from Allah: for (Allah) loveth not those who do wrong. \nوَلَمَنِ انْتَصَرَ بَعْدَ ظُلْمِهٖ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ‏(41)\nWA LAMANISH ANTASARA BA’DA ZULMEH FA-OOLAAA-EKA MAA A’LAYHIM MIN SABEELIN.\nBut indeed if any do help and defend themselves after a wrong (done) to them, against such there is no cause of blame. \nاِنَّمَا السَّبِيْلُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَظْلِمُوْنَ النَّاسَ وَ يَبْغُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(42)\nINNAMAA AS-SABEELU A’LAL LAZEENA YAZLEMOON NAASA WA YABGHOONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQ OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThe blame is only against those who oppress men and wrong-doing and insolently transgress beyond bounds through the land, defying right and justice: for such there will be a penalty grievous. \nوَلَمَنْ صَبَرَ وَغَفَرَ اِنَّ ذٰلِكَ لَمِنْ عَزْمِ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(43)\nWALAMAN SABARA WAGHAFARA INNAL ZAALEKA LAMEN A’AZME AL-AUMOORE.\nBut indeed if any show patience and forgive, that would truly be an exercise of courageous will and resolution in the conduct of affairs. \nوَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ‌ ؕ وَتَرَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ هَلْ اِلٰى مَرَدٍّ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍ‌ۚ‏(44)\nWA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN WALIYYINW MIN BA’DEHI WA TARAL ZAALEMEEN LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA YAQOOLOONA HAL ELAA MARADDIN MIN SABEELIN.\nFor any whom Allah leaves astray, there is no protector thereafter. And thou wilt see the Wrong-doers, when in sight of the Penalty, Say: “Is there any way (to effect) a return?” \nوَتَرٰٮهُمْ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا خٰشِعِيْنَ مِنَ الذُّلِّ يَنْظُرُوْنَ مِنْ طَرْفٍ خَفِىٍّ‌ ؕ وَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَاَهْلِيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ فِىْ عَذَابٍ مُّقِيْمٍ‏(45)\nWA TARAAHUM YUA’RAZOONA A’LAYHAA KHAASHEE’EENA MENAL AZ-ZULLE YANZOROONA MIN TARFIN KHAFEAAAIN WA QAALA LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL KHAASEREEN LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA AHLEEHIM YAWMA QEYAAMATE ALAA INNAL ZAALEMEEN FEE A’ZAABIN MMUQEEMIN.\nAnd thou wilt see them brought forward to the (Penalty), in a humble frame of mind because of (their) disgrace, (and) looking with a stealthy glance. And the Believers will say: “Those are indeed in loss, who have given to perdition their own selves and those belonging to them on the Day of Judgment. Behold! Truly the Wrong-doers are in a lasting Penalty!” \nوَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ يَنْصُرُوْنَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ‏(46)\nWA MAA KAANA LAHUM MIN AAWLEEAAAA YANSOROONAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAH WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN SABEELIN.\nAnd no protectors have they to help them, other than Allah. And for any whom Allah leaves to stray, there is no way (to the Goal). \nاِسْتَجِيْبُوْا لِرَبِّكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ يَوْمٌ لَّا مَرَدَّ لَهٗ مِنَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ مَّلْجَاٍ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّكِيْرٍ‏(47)\nAESTAJEEBOOA LERABBEKUM MIN QABLE AN YAATEYA YAWMUL LAA MARADDA LAHU MENAL LAAH MAA LAKUM MIN MMALJAA YAWMA-EZIN WA MAA LAKUM MIN NNAKEERIN.\nHearken ye to your Lord, before there come a Day which there will be no putting back, because of (the Ordainment of) Allah! that Day there will be for you no place of refuge nor will there be for you any room for denial (of your sins)! \nفَاِنْ اَعْرَضُوْا فَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا‌ؕ اِنْ عَلَيْكَ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّاۤ اِذَاۤ اَذَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنَّا رَحْمَةً فَرِحَ بِهَا‌ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ فَاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ كَفُوْرٌ‏(48)\nFA-IN A-A’RAZOO FAMAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN IN A’LAYKA ILLAA BALAAGHUL WA INNAA EZAA AZAQNAN INSAANA MINNAA RAHMATAM FAREHA BEHAA WA IN TOSIBHUM SAYYE-ATUM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM FA-INNAL INSAANA KAFOORUN.\nIf then they run away, We have not sent thee as a guard over them. Thy duty is but to convey (the Message). And truly, when We give man a taste of a Mercy from Ourselves, he doth exult thereat, but when some ill happens to him, on account of the deeds which his hands have sent forth, truly then is man ungrateful! \nلِّلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ‌ؕ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ ؕ يَهَبُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِنَاثًا وَّيَهَبُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ الذُّكُوْرَ ۙ‏(49)\nLILLAAH MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA YAHABU LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O AENAASAN WWAYAHABU LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O AZ-ZUKOORA.\nTo Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He creates what He wills (and plans). He bestows (children) male or female according to His Will (and Plan), \nاَوْ يُزَوِّجُهُمْ ذُكْرَانًا وَّاِنَاثًا‌ ۚ وَيَجْعَلُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ عَقِيْمًا‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌ قَدِيْرٌ‏(50)\nAW YUZAWJUHUM ZUKRAANAN WWAANAASAN WAYAJA’ALU MAN YASHAAA-O A’AQEEMAN INNAHU A’LEEM QADEER.\nOr He bestows both males and females, and He leaves barren whom He will: for He is full of Knowledge and Power. \nوَمَا كَانَ لِبَشَرٍ اَنْ يُّكَلِّمَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا وَحْيًا اَوْ مِنْ وَّرَآىٴِ حِجَابٍ اَوْ يُرْسِلَ رَسُوْلًا فَيُوْحِىَ بِاِذْنِهٖ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِىٌّ حَكِيْمٌ‏(51)\nWA MAA KAANA LEBASHARIN AN YYUKALLEMAHU LAAHO ILLAA WAHYAN AW MIN WWARAAAA MINW AW YURSELA RASOOLAM FAYOOHEAAA BE-IZNEH MAA YASHAAU INNAHU A’ALEAAAUN HAKEEM.\nIt is not fitting for a man that Allah should speak to him except by inspiration, or from behind a veil, or by the sending of a messenger to reveal, with Allah's permission, what Allah wills: for He is Most High, Most Wise. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ رُوْحًا مِّنْ اَمْرِنَا‌ ؕ مَا كُنْتَ تَدْرِىْ مَا الْكِتٰبُ وَلَا الْاِيْمَانُ وَلٰكِنْ جَعَلْنٰهُ نُوْرًا نَّهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ نَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا‌ ؕ وَاِنَّكَ لَتَهْدِىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍۙ‏(52)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA ROOHAN MIN AAMRENAA MAA KUNTA LAA MAA KETAABO WA LAA AL-AEEMAANU WA LAAKIL LAW NOORAN NNAHDEAA BEHI MAN NNASHAAU MIN E’EBAADENAA WA LATAHDEAA ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd thus have We, by Our Command, sent inspiration to thee: thou knewest not (before) what was Revelation, and what was Faith; but We have made the (Qur'an) a Light, wherewith We guide such of Our servants as We will; and verily thou dost guide (men) to the Straight Way, \nصِرَاطِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اَلَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَصِيْرُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(53)\nSERAATE LAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ ALAA ELAL LAAHE TASEERU OMOOR.\nThe Way of Allah, to Whom belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth. Behold (how) all affairs tend towards Allah! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Shooraa (The Council)\nThis Surah has 53 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be from among those people on whom the angels send salutations and pray for their forgiveness.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah will be raised on the Day of Reckoning with a face as bright as the full moon and he will be told: ‘You are from those who used to recite Surah Shooraa. If you knew the reward for this, you would never have felt tired of reciting it.’ The angels will then be ordered to take him to Paradise where he will find a palace made of red rubies. There will be two huries and a thousand slaves in that palace.\nIf this Surah is written and kept as a talisman, it becomes a means of protection and drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is especially good for those intending to travel as it provides for a journey without unforeseen problems."
